    "blogtextliquid_LBJgtB": {
      "type": "editorial--blog-text-liquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>There is a particular morning in early September when you step outside and the air has changed. It is not cold yet, but the suffocating summer humidity is gone, replaced by a crisp, golden sharpness. Your wardrobe naturally shifts: linen shirts give way to light knitwear, and sandals are replaced by leather boots.</p><p>Your fragrance wardrobe should follow that same seasonal cadence. Fragrances that felt refreshing in ninety-degree heat suddenly feel thin and fleeting in cool autumn breezes, while rich, woody notes that felt too heavy in July now smell glorious.</p>"
      }
    },
